ATHENS, Greece, Nov. 20, 2025 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- Dynagas LNG Partners LP (NYSE: "DLNG") (the "Partnership"), an owner and operator of liquefied natural gas ("LNG") carriers, today announced its results for the three and nine months ended September 30, 2025.
Net Income and Earnings per common unit (basic and diluted) of $45.9 million and $0.99, respectively;
* Adjusted Net Income(1) of $43.0 million and Adjusted Earnings per common unit(1) (basic and diluted) of $0.91;
* Adjusted EBITDA(1) of $82.4 million; and
* 99.5% fleet utilization(2).

The IEEE standard C37.118.2-2011 defines the method and requirements for the transfer of synchrophasors in the context of SGs [30,31];
The IEC 61850 standard defines the exchange of data between IEDs for substation automation [32]. The standard was initially designed for communication within a substation, but later evolved to enable substations to communicate with each other [32];
IEC 62056 was defined for the transmission of smart metering data, including protocols for communication over power lines [32].

